WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.322
- All right, everybody, welcome back.

00:00:01.322 --> 00:00:04.896
All hour we're celebrating
food, glorious food.

00:00:04.896 --> 00:00:07.090
Now I wanted to take a break
from my kitchen classes

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:09.120
to introduce you to an
awesome girl, making her mark

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.000
in the culinary world.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.082
She just put out a cookbook,

00:00:13.082 --> 00:00:15.220
but instead of making money from it,

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.380
she's giving all the proceeds

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.170
to help keep people fed,

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.430
which is such a beautiful thing.

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:20.263
Good heart.

00:00:20.263 --> 00:00:22.300
She's exactly the kind of overachiever

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.911
our friends at Pilot
makers of the G2 jelly pen,

00:00:24.911 --> 00:00:26.810
the go-to pin of the Kelly Clarkson show,

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:28.310
like to help us celebrate.

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:31.020
So let's welcome the
author of "Bake Away,"

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:32.527
18 year old Sahana.

00:00:32.527 --> 00:00:33.485
(crowd cheering)

00:00:33.485 --> 00:00:34.999
- Hi.

00:00:34.999 --> 00:00:37.370
So, 18 years old.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.209
You're so young.

00:00:38.209 --> 00:00:40.300
This is such a huge accomplishment

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:41.133
for someone so young

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:42.840
and then to have such a great heart

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:43.810
at giving back, like,

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:44.900
has this always been a dream

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:45.850
to do a book like this?

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:46.905
- Yeah, thank you so much.

00:00:46.905 --> 00:00:49.854
Yeah, ever since I was four or five.

00:00:49.854 --> 00:00:52.860
My parents are avid cooks,
so I've been in the kitchen.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:54.170
I grew up around it,

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:57.300
and I've always been inspired to bake.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:01.450
We had a cookbook shelf in our home

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:03.294
and had recipes all over the world,

00:01:03.294 --> 00:01:05.260
Thai food, Mexican food, Indian food.

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:06.093
My family is Indian.

00:01:06.093 --> 00:01:07.985
So we cooked a lot of Indian food,

00:01:07.985 --> 00:01:12.985
and yeah, my favorite
cookbook is by Curtis Stone,

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:16.280
and so I did his fish tacos,

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:19.030
and his apple pie really
got me into baking.

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:20.650
- [Kelly] Oh, girl, I love apple pie.

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:21.880
- [Sahana] Yeah.

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:23.440
- Apple pie is so good, y'all,

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.650
especially when it's done so nicely.

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:26.644
My mouth is watering.

00:01:26.644 --> 00:01:28.920
So you've also been dedicated

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.690
to tackling food insecurity,

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:32.130
and it says for your whole life.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:33.040
You're so young though

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.470
to have this big of an issue

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:35.570
in your head and your heart,

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:37.090
to be tackling is such a cool thing.

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:38.730
So why is this so important to you?

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:40.180
- Yeah, thank you.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:41.557
So growing up,

00:01:41.557 --> 00:01:43.160
around the same age I started baking,

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:44.171
around four or five,

00:01:44.171 --> 00:01:47.470
I volunteered at a local
women's and children's shelter

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:49.920
with my mom, and we baked and served,

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.440
and ate the enchiladas we made

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:52.630
with the women there,

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:54.248
and that's really what got me exposed

00:01:54.248 --> 00:01:56.230
to the food insecurity problem

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:57.600
in the area I grew up in,

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.490
and then in high school,

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:02.670
I worked with UNICEF
and I lobbied Congress

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:04.920
with a group of other UNICEF members

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:08.160
where we advocated for the
Global Child Thrive Act

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.830
and thankfully it got passed,

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:13.163
and now--
(crowd cheering)

00:02:13.163 --> 00:02:16.330
Now a lot of children across the world

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:20.203
have increased access
to nutrition programs,

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:23.360
water, and vaccines,

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:25.090
and then now in college,

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:27.350
I work at the FRESH Basic
Needs Hub at UC Irvine

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:31.679
where we stock produce and
groceries for college students,

00:02:31.679 --> 00:02:33.862
and for residents of Irvine.

00:02:33.862 --> 00:02:36.018
(crowd cheering)

00:02:36.018 --> 00:02:40.153
- I mean, you're 18 years old.

00:02:40.153 --> 00:02:43.743
Like, I feel like I was
just a horrible person.

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:45.847
I feel like, "Oh my God,

00:02:45.847 --> 00:02:48.549
"if we all were you, like how
much the world would be better

00:02:48.549 --> 00:02:50.377
"if we tackled all these things that

00:02:50.377 --> 00:02:52.190
you're already tackling,

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:53.360
it's amazing.
- Thank you so much.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:55.310
- And it's amazing that it was...

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:56.163
It's just been set on your heart

00:02:56.163 --> 00:02:58.323
and you've ran with it.

00:02:58.323 --> 00:03:00.520
Imagine all the people you've helped

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:01.560
and you're so young.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:03.140
So tell us about your cookbook.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:05.150
Tell us about this, "Bake Away."

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:06.160
- My freshman year of high school,

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:07.440
I really got into writing

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.930
and it became another passion
of mine alongside baking,

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:13.240
and so I wanted to combine
both of them into a cookbook

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:16.590
and I ended up immediately
drafting the recipes

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:20.330
and taking photographs
of the recipes I made

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:22.700
in my kitchen in my dining room,

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:25.410
and I finally completed a manuscript,

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:26.990
like a a draft of the manuscript,

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:29.410
and then I reached out to a publisher.

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:30.243
I worked with them

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:32.000
with the editing and publishing process,

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.450
and after that I decided I felt a duty

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:36.990
to donate to No Kid Hungry,

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:38.080
and I started working with them,

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:40.240
and right now we're really, really close

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.723
to reaching our goal which is $50,000

00:03:41.723 --> 00:03:43.833
and 500,000 meals for kids.

00:03:44.678 --> 00:03:45.511
- Wow.

00:03:46.636 --> 00:03:49.160
- You're such a remarkable human.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:52.720
I feel like we can all be
better humans in this moment.

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:54.800
So we love what you're doing,

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.126
but we're hardly the only ones.

00:03:56.126 --> 00:03:57.670
In fact, we've got someone here

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.140
who wants to congratulate you

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:01.180
on all you've accomplished already.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.290
So let's bring him out.

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:03.798
Chef Curtis Stone.

00:04:03.798 --> 00:04:06.593
(crowd cheering)

00:04:06.593 --> 00:04:08.593
- Oh my God.
- Oh my God.

00:04:10.318 --> 00:04:11.609
- You're amazing.
- Oh my God,

00:04:11.609 --> 00:04:13.427
thank you so much.

00:04:13.427 --> 00:04:14.929
Thank you so much.

00:04:14.929 --> 00:04:16.507
- You're incredible.

00:04:16.507 --> 00:04:18.737
- Thank you.
- Have a seat, have a seat.

00:04:18.737 --> 00:04:19.640
- Oh my God, thank you so much.

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:23.200
- There's people all over
this country right now

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.000
that are going over there,

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.440
and if you're not, you should be.

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.820
You should be going onto your laptop

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:28.670
and ordering your book.

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:30.310
- Thank you so much.
- Because what you are doing

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:31.574
is a beautiful, beautiful thing.

00:04:31.574 --> 00:04:32.640
- Thank you.

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:35.019
- No, it's amazing.
- And at such a young age,

00:04:35.019 --> 00:04:36.670
like, you know what I'm saying?

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:39.270
I feel like we weren't
doing stuff like that

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:40.240
for people at 18.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:42.080
I mean, I hope I was doing something,

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:42.913
but I...

00:04:42.913 --> 00:04:45.423
Wow, like what do you wanna say to Sahana?

00:04:45.423 --> 00:04:46.835
- I wanna say congratulations.

00:04:46.835 --> 00:04:48.310
- Thank you so much.
- What you've done is

00:04:48.310 --> 00:04:49.510
absolutely incredible,

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:50.670
and I've got a couple more friends

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:51.503
to meet you too.

00:04:51.503 --> 00:04:53.292
- Okay.
- All of my fellow Iron Chefs.

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:54.342
Come on out, guys!

00:04:54.342 --> 00:04:56.183
- Come on out!

00:04:56.183 --> 00:04:57.603
(crowd cheering)

00:04:57.603 --> 00:04:59.339
Everybody, it's Iron Chefs--

00:04:59.339 --> 00:05:02.089
(crowd cheering)

00:05:04.082 --> 00:05:05.343
- Thank you.

00:05:05.343 --> 00:05:06.684
- Wow.
- Oh my God,

00:05:06.684 --> 00:05:08.221
thank you so much.

00:05:08.221 --> 00:05:09.914
- You're so amazing.
- Oh my gosh.

00:05:09.914 --> 00:05:11.465
I was like, "What?"
- Congratulations.

00:05:11.465 --> 00:05:13.597
- Thank you so much.
- What a decent human.

00:05:13.597 --> 00:05:15.062
- Thank you.

00:05:15.062 --> 00:05:16.817
- Oh my gosh.

00:05:16.817 --> 00:05:19.165
- Oh my God, thank you so much.

00:05:19.165 --> 00:05:22.270
- Everybody, our partners at Pilot,

00:05:22.270 --> 00:05:24.970
makers of the G2 jelly
pen want to honor you

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.370
as the overachiever you are.

00:05:26.370 --> 00:05:28.610
So they are donating $5,000

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:32.165
in your name to No Kid Hungry.
- Thank you so much.

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:32.998
- Oh my God.

00:05:32.998 --> 00:05:35.500
Thank you so much, Sahana, truly.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:37.910
It's so funny, everybody always says

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:38.880
you can't learn from the young.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.060
We can learn so much from the young.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:41.720
You're such a pure heart.
- Thank you so much.

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:43.530
- And you're doing so much
good for so many people.

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:44.707
Thank you so much for
sharing this with us.

00:05:44.707 --> 00:05:45.915
- Thank you so much

00:05:45.915 --> 00:05:47.375
for having me.
- Yeah!

